From 487ccc22e5ee583f4768fed870670adeebd934f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:31:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] pm: a fresh HERMES_HOME links the account's verified
 tools, uv cache and source snapshot

A test, review or mutation home (HERMES_HOME=<scratch>, real HOME) downloaded
and unpacked every tool (~1.5 GiB), kept its own uv cache (~400 MiB) that its
environments hard-linked into, compiled ~70 MiB of bytecode per environment and
copied ~67 MiB of source per generation: ~2.1 GiB per home (27 GiB of
toolchains on worker-2's done-card workspaces).

pm.environments.account_home_root() names the account's default home when the
active home is another one on the same filesystem. Such a home now:
- links each tool entry from the account store when it records the same pin
  (version + target + artifact sha256s); the linked tree must hash to the
  recorded digest, else it is dropped and the pin downloads as before. A link
  that cannot be made copies; Windows always copies; cross-target stages never
  link.
- shares the account's uv cache (content-keyed, uv-locked), so environments
  link into it instead of a per-home cache.
- skips --compile-bytecode for its own installs/ environments (modules compile
  on first import).
- links unchanged source-snapshot files from the account's selected generation
  for the same checkout (or its own hermes-agent), compared byte-for-byte and
  by mode.

Proof: HERMES_HOME=$(mktemp -d) scripts/run-in-hermes-env true on worker-6:
tools 0 MiB and installs 7.4 MiB of nlink=1 files (9 s); a --shared clone at
main~3: tools 0, installs 9.8 MiB, no cache/uv (15 s). Before: 1.5 GiB tools +
603 MiB installs + 392 MiB cache/uv. tests/pm/test_account_seed.py: 18 tests,
RED on main (11 fail), 16/16 condition mutants killed.
